From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yodaliu <yodaliu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:32:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] sound: usb: qmi: fix period size/count and set
 altsetting before endpoint setup

Constrain offload streams to 480-frame periods x 8 and select the data
endpoint altsetting before configuring it.

Reconstructed from the stock FiiO M21 FW 1.1.0 module by disassembly
comparison; the rebuilt module matches the stock one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/usb/usb_audio_qmi_svc.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/usb_audio_qmi_svc.c b/sound/usb/usb_audio_qmi_svc.c
index ff7ec3a0115..b7efff7198e 100644
--- a/sound/usb/usb_audio_qmi_svc.c
+++ b/sound/usb/usb_audio_qmi_svc.c
@@ -1359,6 +1359,11 @@ static int configure_endpoints(struct snd_usb_audio *chip,
 {
 	int err;
 
+	/* select the data endpoint's altsetting before configuring it */
+	if (subs->data_endpoint)
+		usb_set_interface(chip->dev, subs->data_endpoint->iface,
+				  subs->data_endpoint->altsetting);
+
 	if (subs->data_endpoint->need_setup) {
 		err = snd_usb_endpoint_configure(chip, subs->data_endpoint);
 		if (err < 0) {
@@ -1474,6 +1479,10 @@ static int enable_audio_stream(struct snd_usb_substream *subs,
 			channels, 0);
 	_snd_pcm_hw_param_set(&params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_RATE,
 			cur_rate, 0);
+	_snd_pcm_hw_param_set(&params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIOD_SIZE,
+			480, 0);
+	_snd_pcm_hw_param_set(&params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIODS,
+			8, 0);
 
 	if (!chip->intf[0])
 		return -ENODEV;
